      "id": "sol.amc-8-1989-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Each fraction is a decimal in a different place: \\(\\frac{2}{10} = 0.2,\\) \\(\\frac{4}{100} = 0.04,\\) and \\(\\frac{6}{1000} = 0.006.\\)\n\nAdding these gives \\(0.2 + 0.04 + 0.006 = 0.246.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D .",
